criptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-12T14:21:04Z","updated_at":"2022-07-12T14:32:57Z","body":"With the code as written above, this seems like intended behavior. But it seems like a real issue is being described.\r\n\r\nI would expect a system like this to only print \"activated\" when there are keyboard input changes, but this currently happens on every frame.\r\n\r\n```rs\r\nfn keyboard(keyboard: Res<Input<KeyCode>>) {\r\n    if !keyboard.is_changed() {\r\n        return;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    info!(\"activated\");\r\n}\r\n``` \r\n\r\nThis seems like a reasonable thing to want to do for e.g. a \"Press any key\" screen.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1181822129/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rparrett","id":200550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett","html_url":"https://github.com/rparrett","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1181837225","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292#issuecomment-1181837225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292","id":1181837225,"node_id":"IC_kwDODf6-U85GcWep","user":{"login":"rparrett","id":200550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett","html_url":"https://github.com/rparrett","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-12T14:33:15Z","updated_at":"2022-07-12T14:34:54Z","body":"\"Press any key\" would probably be better accomplished like this though:\r\n\r\n```rs\r\nfn keyboard(keyboard: Res<Input<KeyCode>>) {\r\n    if keyboard.get_just_pressed().next().is_none() {\r\n        return;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    info!(\"activated\");\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1181837225/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rparrett","id":200550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett","html_url":"https://github.com/rparrett","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1181907665","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292#issuecomment-1181907665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292","id":1181907665,"node_id":"IC_kwDODf6-U85GcnrR","user":{"login":"ruibinx","id":13186159,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTg2MTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13186159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx","html_url":"https://github.com/ruibinx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-12T15:26:49Z","updated_at":"2022-07-12T15:26:49Z","body":"> With the code as written above, this seems like intended behavior. But it seems like a real issue is being described.\r\n> \r\n> I would expect a system like this to only print \"activated\" when there are keyboard input changes, but this currently happens on every frame.\r\n> \r\n> ```rust\r\n> fn keyboard(keyboard: Res<Input<KeyCode>>) {\r\n>     if !keyboard.is_changed() {\r\n>         return;\r\n>     }\r\n> \r\n>     info!(\"activated\");\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> This seems like a reasonable thing to want to do for e.g. a \"Press any key\" screen.\r\n\r\nUnlike the provided example which has only a single keyboard resource param, the actual code in my game is:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nfn keyboard(keyboard: Res<Input<KeyCode>>, some_query: Query<&SomeComponent1, &SomeComponent2>) {\r\n     if keyboard.just_pressed(keycode1) {\r\n            do_sth()\r\n     } else if ..{\r\n            do_sth()\r\n     } else  {\r\n            ...\r\n     }\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm kind of worried about the `some_query` part, if resource change detection should happen inside the system, would that mean the query would be made every frame thus may slow downthe whole game ?\r\n\r\nI'm new to bevy and ECS and game dev, so please correct me if I'm wrong.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1181907665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ruibinx","id":13186159,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTg2MTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13186159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx","html_url":"https://github.com/ruibinx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruibinx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1182013702","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292#issuecomment-1182013702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292","id":1182013702,"node_id":"IC_kwDODf6-U85GdBkG","user":{"login":"rparrett","id":200550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett","html_url":"https://github.com/rparrett","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-12T16:57:23Z","updated_at":"2022-07-12T16:58:06Z","body":"> I'm kind of worried about the some_query part, if resource change detection should happen inside the system, would that mean the query would be made every frame thus may slow downthe whole game ?\r\n\r\nQueries should be cheap to create, so you probably don't to be worrying about that.\r\n\r\nIt's possible to prevent a system from running with [Run Criteria](https://bevy-cheatbook.github.io/programming/run-criteria.html) but there are some caveats and that would be a bit of a micro-optimization.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1182013702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rparrett","id":200550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett","html_url":"https://github.com/rparrett","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparrett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/1182848476","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292#issuecomment-1182848476","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/5292","id":